# CMS — Admin-Editable Front-End Content
## Implementation Plan for TaxProConsult

---

> **Goal**: Every piece of text and media visible to public users on the website (hero sections, About Us, FAQ, navigation labels, calls-to-action, etc.) is stored in the database, multi-language, and editable live from the Admin dashboard — just like Amazon, Shopify, or WordPress, but purpose-built for your stack.

---

## 1. How Amazon / Big Sites Do It (The Pattern)

Amazon and similar platforms use a concept called a **Content Management System (CMS)** backed by a **Key-Value content store** in the database. The core idea is simple:

```
Every piece of UI text has a unique KEY.
The database maps that KEY → a VALUE per LANGUAGE.
The frontend reads from the DB, not from hardcoded strings.
The admin can update the VALUE at any time.
```

For example, instead of hardcoding:
```jsx
<h1>Welcome to TaxProConsult</h1>
```

It becomes:
```jsx
<h1>{content["hero.title"]}</h1>  // reads from DB, in current language
```

