  hooks/
    useSiteContent.js           ← Simple hook (NEW)
  lib/
    api.js                      ← Add siteContentApi (EXTEND EXISTING)
  pages/
    admin/
      SiteContentTab.jsx        ← New admin tab (NEW)
  components/
    admin/
      ContentEditor.jsx         ← Rich inline editor for text/html/image/json (NEW)
      ContentSection.jsx        ← Groups keys by section (NEW)
```

### 5.2 `SiteContentContext.jsx` — Global CMS Provider

```jsx
// Fetches ALL content once, provides it everywhere via context
// Frontend usage: const { c } = useSiteContent();
// Then: <h1>{c("hero.title")}</h1>

const SiteContentContext = createContext({});

export const SiteContentProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const { locale } = useLanguage();

  const { data: content = {} } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ["site-content", locale],
    queryFn: () => siteContentApi.list(locale),
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,  // Cache 5 min — fast page loads
  });

  // c("hero.title") → returns live DB value or fallback
  const c = (key, fallback = "") => content[key] ?? fallback;

  return (
    <SiteContentContext.Provider value={{ c, content }}>
      {children}
    </SiteContentContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

### 5.3 Updating `Index.jsx` / `Services.jsx` / etc.

Replace hardcoded strings with `c("key")` calls:

```jsx
// BEFORE (hardcoded):
<h1 className="hero-title">Welcome to TaxProConsult</h1>
<p>Your trusted tax advisory firm</p>

// AFTER (CMS-driven):
const { c } = useSiteContent();
<h1 className="hero-title">{c("hero.title", "Welcome to TaxProConsult")}</h1>
<p>{c("hero.subtitle", "Your trusted tax advisory firm")}</p>
```

> **Note:** The fallback argument ensures the page never appears blank if the admin hasn't set a value yet.

### 5.4 Admin `SiteContentTab.jsx` — The Editor Interface

The admin sees content grouped by section (Hero, About, FAQ, etc.). For each key, they can:

1. **Select a language tab** (EN | SW | ZH — from your live Languages list)
2. **Edit the value** in the appropriate editor:
   - `text` → Simple `<Input>` field
   - `html` → A rich text area (or simple textarea with HTML preview)
   - `image` → File upload with current image preview
   - `json` → Structured editor (e.g., for FAQ items: add/remove Q&A pairs)
3. **Click Save** → Calls `PUT /site-content/{id}/translations`
4. **See live preview** → Changes reflect instantly on the public site (after React Query cache invalidation)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SITE CONTENT                                    + Add Section  │
│  Dashboard / Site Content / List                                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  [EN]  [SW]  [ZH]   ← Language Tabs                           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ▼ Hero Section                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐           │
│  │ hero.badge    [text]  [Your Trusted Partner  ✏] │           │
│  │ hero.title    [text]  [Welcome to TaxProC... ✏] │           │
│  │ hero.subtitle [html]  [Your trusted tax adv ✏] │           │
│  │ hero.image    [img]   [🖼 hero-image.jpg   📤] │           │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘           │
│  ▼ About Section                                                │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐           │
│  │ about.title   [text]  [About Us             ✏] │           │
│  │ about.body    [html]  [We are a leading...  ✏] │           │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘           │
